OK, my guy is two weaponing (skilled) a +3 elven dagger
(expert) and a +0 long sword (basic). If I understand the
above, leading with the dagger, in addition to the +3
enchantment and +2 "to hit" for all daggers, the two weapon
penalty is -5 since the two weapon skill is less than the
dagger. So the net for leading with the dagger is zero.

If I lead with the long sword, the two weapon penalty is -7
(long sword skill less than two weapon) and no bonus for
enchantment or the weapon "to hit" applies.

So for this character, THAC0 is 17 (other factors omitted
for simplicity) leading with the dagger and 10 leading with
the long sword!

That's counter intuitive!
